          %h3#nonexample (Non)example
          %p
            Let
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rel"} REL
            be the (locally posetal) 2-category of sets and relations. A monad on a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is just an endorelation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            satisfying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi X
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_X\subseteq R
            (reflexivity) and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\circ R \subseteq R
            (transitivity) i.e. a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            arises from an adjunction it is necessarily of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R=F\circ F^{op}
            implying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R=R^{op}
            (symmetry) since adjunctions in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi REL
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} REL
            consist of functional relations as the left adjoint with their opposite relation as right adjoint. In other words, only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relations
            admit Eilenberg–Moore objects which then consist of the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^R
            of equivalence classes with “free algebra functor”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^R
            relating
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            to its equivalence class
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x]\in X^R
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#universal_properties Universal properties
          %p
            Apart from being the universal left
            = succeed "-module," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            has some other interesting properties.
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi RAdj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RAdj(C)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat/C
            on the functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to C
            that have
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints"} left adjoints
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            there is a full subcategory of this consisting of the adjoint pairs that compose to give
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^T \colon C^T \to C
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            of this category.
          %h3#AsColimitCompletionOfKleisliCategory As a colimit completion of the Kleisli category
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\nu)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
              of the first stage of its
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+resolution"} bar resolution
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 2
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mi ν
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (T^2 A, \mu_{T A})
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\mu_A}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{T \nu}{\longrightarrow}}
                    (T A, \mu_A)
                    \\stackrel{\nu}{\longrightarrow}
                    (A,\nu)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+coequalizer"} reflexive coequalizer
              of
              = succeed "-algebras." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fork"} fork
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+coequalizer"} split coequalizer
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+coequalizer"} absolute coequalizer
              (sometimes called the
              = succeed "," do
                %em Beck coequalizer
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+monadicity+theorem"} Beck monadicity theorem
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 2
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mrow
                            %mi T
                            %mi A
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T^2 A  \stackrel{\eta_{T A}}{\longleftarrow} T A \stackrel{\eta_A}{\longleftarrow} A
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#MacLane"} MacLane, bottom of p. 148 and exercise 4 on p. 151
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "split+coequalizer#BeckCoequalizerForAlgebrasOverAMonad"} split coequalizer – Beck coequalizer for algebras over a monad
          %p
            In particular this says that every
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
