                = succeed "," do
                  %em Yoneda structures
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 50
            %li#AM24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathanael+Arkor"}> Nathanael Arkor
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dylan+McDermott"} Dylan McDermott
                %em The pullback theorem for relative monads
                (2024) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.01281"}> arXiv:2404.01281
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The formal theory of monads II
              %p
                %strong 175
                1–3 (2002) 243-265 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049(02)00137-8"}> doi:10.1016/S0022-4049(02)00137-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} local presentability
            of EM-categories:
          %ul
            %li#AdamekRosicky
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Ad%C3%A1mek"}> Jiří Adámek
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locally+presentable+and+accessible+categories"} Locally presentable and accessible categories
          %p
            The following paper of Melliès compares the representability condition of (
            %a{:href => "#Linton69"}> Linton 69
            ) with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+condition"} Segal condition
            that distinguishes those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            that are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerves"} nerves
            of categories.
          %ul
            %li#Mellies10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul-Andr%C3%A9+Melli%C3%A8s"}> Paul-André Melliès
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Segal condition meets computational effects
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.pps.jussieu.fr/~mellies/papers/segal-lics-2010.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The example of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monads"} idempotent monads
            is discussed also in
          %ul#Borceux
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            as the final adjoint decomposition of the monad:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Voutas"}> Anthony Voutas
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The basic theory of monads and their connection to universal algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://voutasaur.us/monad-algebra.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Voutas-Monads.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-monads"} (infinity,1)-monads
            realized in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            is around def. 6.1.7 of
          %ul#RiehlVerity13
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"} Dominic Verity
              %em Homotopy coherent adjunctions and the formal theory of monads
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.8279"}> arXiv:1310.8279
              )
          %p
            An analogue of the pullback theorem for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+algebras"} lax algebras
            (there confusingly called “pseudoagebras”) of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            is given in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Burroni"}> Albert Burroni
              \.
              = succeed "." do
                %em Structures pseudo-algébriques (1ère partie)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/CTGDC_1975__16_4_343_0.pdf"} pdf
        .revisedby
